<title>POLAND: POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 6.0 PCT IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 6.0 PCT IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output</p>
<p>(unadjusted) rose 6.0 percent in April after a 6.4 percent rise</p>
<p>in March, and was 15.9 percent higher than in April 1996, the</p>
<p>Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Industrial output rose 9.8 percent in the January-April</p>
<p>period.</p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT     APRIL     MARCH	APRIL 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	6.0     6.4   (6.6)     -4.4</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)	     15.9     4.6   (4.8)     15.2</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100) 135.4     N/A (128.0)    120.3</p>
<p> mining m/m change		 4.7    -1.7  (-2.4)    -10.0</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change	     2.7   -11.7 (-12.4)	3.8</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	7.4     8.1   (8.4)     -1.5</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change   18.5     8.7   (9.0)     18.4</p>
<p> utilities m/m change	   -4.2    -0.2   (0.0)    -19.2</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	  5.9   -10.7 (-10.5)	2.7</p>
<p>NOTES - Revised data in brackets. April 1997 had 23 working</p>
<p>days, March 1997 had 21 and April 1996 had 22 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
